<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n64265" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λυτρ-όω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>release on receipt of a ransom, hold to ransom</i>,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινὰ χρημάτων ὅσων δοκεῖ</span>
			<i>for</i> such a sum as is agreed on, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Tht.</u>
				165e
			</span></i>; <i>redeem</i> a pledge, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λ. τὰ ἱμάτια</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>POxy.</u>
					530.14
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(ii A. D.)</span>, etc.:—
				Med.
			, <i>release by payment of ransom, redeem</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρὰ τῶν Αἰτωλῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					12(5).36
				</span></i>
			 (Naxos, <span class="entity">iii B. C.</span>), cf. <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Ex.</u>
				13.15
			</span></i>, al.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὴν χώραν χρημάτων οὐκ ὀλίγων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					18.16.1
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡμᾶς ἀπὸ πάσης ἀνομίας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Ep.Tit.</u>
					2.14
				</span></i>
			:—
				Pass.
			, <i>to be ransomed</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκ τῶν ἰδίων λελυτρῶσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					19.170
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>EN</u>
				1164b34
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἵματι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>1 Ep.Pet.</u>
					1.18
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Pass.
			, <i>to be released</i> from an obligation, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PEleph.</u>
				19.8
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii B. C.)</span>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b> mistranslation of Hebr. '<i>rp</i> 'break the neck',
				<i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Ex.</u>
				13.13
			</span></i>. -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ών</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῶνος</span>, ὁ, 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπόπατος</span>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				2
			</span></i>, ib.<i><span class="en">
				<u>4 Ki.</u>
				10.27
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AB</u>
				433
			</span></i>.</div>
